 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
+- Freezing: only a manager of the project may freeze it (other members → 403,
+  org admins without a role → 403, not readable → 404, archived → 409). A freeze
+  changes every member's role to `viewer`, managers included, and returns the
+  members. Nobody can change a frozen project's tasks afterwards, because no one
+  has a writer role any more (writes → 403). Reads still work. There is no
+  endpoint that undoes a freeze or adds members. Freezing again needs the
+  manager role, which the freeze removed, so a second freeze by the same
+  caller → 403.
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
